      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "I GOT CHILLS NZ (3) was a beaten favourite last start but he had the outside barrier and locked wheels so was far from disgraced when beaten 5m. Led to win from this barrier prior, part of a string of wins and placings he had put together at this circuit and distance. The draw gives him the chance to return to the winners' list. The same could be said for BUZZ BOMB (2) who drew wide and raced parked but fought well to go under narrowly last time. Led from this barrier to win at this circuit and distance prior, albeit in a lower-graded race. He has the speed to take advantage of the draw and make an impact again. VITE MONET (8) cops a wide barrier but has been tackling stronger company of late. Won the last time he raced in this grade so is better placed. ACTION MAJOR NZ (1) has won two of three starts so far this time in, the latest from this barrier. Stronger here but he can be competitive.",
